{"id": "EUVD-2026-93115", "enisaUuid": "d17f3197-08d0-3b61-a975-feacc4cb1393", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: p54: require a full exp_if record in PDR_INTERFACE_LIST\n\nThe PDR_INTERFACE_LIST loop only checks that the record start is within\nthe entry before reading an entire struct exp_if from it. A truncated\ntrailing record makes the if_id/variant reads cross the entry boundary\ninto the heap beyond the EEPROM buffer (verified with a KASAN\nreproducer of the loop). The variant also feeds the synth front-end\nselection, so this is not only a leak.\n\nAdvance only while a full record still fits in the entry.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:18", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/162dbe1c285a621eab6a9f2851086b63a0378928", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/70bf34b425fe549a4f6a8d50a319f8f05d1f91c9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/487f966421014de41e835bbce3feb30b35f4f729", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bc83c04be042f53869c315b8e1eb5f124959d1d7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d44c1badc2dcb042985f7e37f4c448c84548b81f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d2fb6b588dc5bbab4f603661e41cd60f0d931628", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d82492fd0a3fb61963c236521852763238ad3898", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d8efd84f49379ed28624098821f80e992657d935"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98187", "GHSA-mr98-38q8-fvr3"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "04a852bc-d51c-3f27-a779-62adb0707008", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "05a63cba-caab-371a-870d-c19ef7e429bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eff1a59c48e3c6a006eb4fe5f2e405a996f2259d <d8efd84f49379ed28624098821f80e992657d935"}, {"id": "0b01c38f-beea-337a-87bd-f9de486ed720", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "eff1a59c